First Author: Glass
Title: A machine learning algorithm improves the diagnostic accuracy of the histologic component of antibody mediated rejection (AMR-H) in cardiac transplant endomyocardial biopsies
Source number: 15

Very short summary: This retrospective pathology study developed a deep-learning image-classification model to diagnose the histologic component of antibody-mediated rejection (pAMR-H) in cardiac transplant biopsies. Five key findings were: (1) 4,212 annotated image regions were generated from 300 H&E slides; (2) the model used a ResNet50 convolutional neural network with transfer learning; (3) overall validation accuracy across four classes was 98%; (4) pAMR-H was distinguished from normal myocardium, healing injury, and acute cellular rejection with very high accuracy and AUCs around 0.992–0.995; and (5) human pathologist agreement was substantially lower, especially when pAMR-H co-occurred with healing injury or mixed rejection. Figures 1–3 and the methods/results text were used directly for this extraction.

