	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: The study used annotated H&E pathology image patches and a “convolutional neural network approach utilizing transfer learning.” The ResNet50 model was initialized with pretrained weights and fine-tuned. The model was compared against blinded human pathologist review in a separate curated set of slides. Regions of interest were manually annotated by experts, which functions as manual/clinical feature selection at the region level. Training settings including Adam optimizer, learning rate 0.0001, cross-entropy loss, and stopping on validation-loss plateau were reported.

Section 4: AI Quality & Reproducibility (CONVINCE Standards)
	•	Missing Data Handling: Not Reported
	•	Class Imbalance Addressed: No
	•	Code Availability: No
	•	Data Preprocessing / Normalization Described: Yes
	•	Training Size (N): 2948
	•	Test Size (N): 842
	•	Section 4 Comments/Quotes: The dataset contained 4,212 annotations split 70%/10%/20% into training, validation, and testing. That corresponds to approximately 2,948 training annotations and 842 test annotations. The four classes were balanced at 1,053 regions each, so explicit class-imbalance correction was not reported and was likely unnecessary. Preprocessing was described through de-identification, whole-slide scanning at 40X, annotation, extraction of non-overlapping 224×224 windows, and train/validation/test splitting. Code availability was not reported. Missing-data handling was not relevant to image patches and was not described.

